															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/boogey-man23" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2362395); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2362395&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606378968" alt="Boogey_Man23" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2362395)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/boogey-man23" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2362395); return false;" >Boogey_Man23</a></span> <span class="odate time_1597473585 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">15 Aug 2020 06:39</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4747906">
									

<p>From the guys who brought you the SCP about the firetruck that came to life. Get ready for… More big trucks that come to life!</p>
<p>In this, the latest <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/boogey-man23" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2362395); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2362395&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1604566347" alt="Boogey_Man23" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2362395)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/boogey-man23" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2362395); return false;">Boogey_Man23</a></span> &amp; <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/nickthebrick1" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5208936); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5208936&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1604566347" alt="Nickthebrick1" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5208936)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/nickthebrick1" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5208936); return false;">Nickthebrick1</a></span> Production!</p>
<hr />
<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Not necessary.</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">SCP Article</span> Tale</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Action-Thriller / Heist Caper story</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Typical narrative fiction style</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> In a city where garbage is piling up in the streets, <em>&quot;one man's trash is another man's treasure&quot;</em>. Someone with the means to convert garbage into profits is planning to get rich in one big move, and they're doing the heist&#8230; with anomalous sapient big trucks!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">So&nbsp;what's&nbsp;the&nbsp;scoop?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Alright,&nbsp;listen&nbsp;close.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> When one phase of the scheme gets picked up on the Foundation's radar, a pair of Field Agents are sent to investigate. They follow a breadcrumb trail of clues that leads them to uncover the whole plot - but can they resolve the situation and catch the mastermind before it's too late?</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> A team of heavy commercial vehicles that are alive and working together to pull off an unconventional caper, and the Foundation has to figure it out and contain the situation before it's too late.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Meet the Caper Crew!</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>DIVA-SCENT:</strong> A rubbish bin that people perceive to be a nice young girl. She's the influential face of the bunch that's going to have civillians unwittingly aiding the rest of the team.</li>
<li><strong>STAKE &amp; SPIKE:</strong> A deck-bed cargo truck and a forklift that work together as a duo. They're a pair of tough guys with a supporting role in the scheme.</li>
<li><strong>DUSTER:</strong> Slow, steady, and smart; a streetsweeping truck who's been casing all the curbsides in the city, plotting the routes for the team on the night of the heist.</li>
<li><strong>TWO-PAIRS:</strong> A fearless dump truck that's ready to haul a heavy load, and to get heavyhanded with anything trying to interfere in the plot.</li>
<li><strong>BEARD:</strong> A garbage truck, he is the team's cunning leader. Actually has the ability to convert the loaded trash into valuables.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<hr />
<p>We have got some plans staked out for how the plot kicks off and unfolds, but for now mainly judging audience interest / seeking feedback on the premise. Thanks!</p>

