			<div class="content" id="post-content-4751536">
									

<p>This feels like it might work better as a tale than a SCP just from the perspective of it allowing you to really centre the story on the people carrying out the heist instead of the Foundation? Like I can see it being a fun multi-perspective story where you alternate PoVs between the Foundation racing to catch the SCPs and the trucks; so you can really ramp the tension up that way.</p>
<p>Beyond this, I guess I'm just. unsure on the specifics? Like, if trash is so valuable, why aren't they robbing landfill sites instead of garbage from a city? Why are they using sapient garbage trucks instead of like, normal ones? I guess the implication is it's cos the entire heist crew are the trucks?</p>
<hr />
<p>On a higher level note, this seems very much like it could be fun even if I'm not quite sure how you'd pull it off (in a neutral way: it seems like you haven't planned this rather; and i'm not saying I don't see anyway it could be pulled off); and like. the devil is in the detail I guess; I'd be unwilling to greenlight this without having a better idea of how you'd be intending actually telling the story.</p>

							</div>

								
					
